__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# Deformed assets written by the example. `--out` can point anywhere, so this is
# by extension rather than by directory.
*.ply

# ── tracked by exception: the sample asset ──────────────────────────────────
# `data/penguin_original.ply` is 5.6 MB and the penguin example cannot run
# without it. GitHub's per-file limit is 100 MB, so tracking it is simply fine —
# and it is the difference between a bare clone that runs the example and one
# that only reads about it, which is the whole point of this repository. The
# method repo's CONTEXT.md listed Git LFS and a fetch script as candidate
# workarounds for a constraint that does not exist; that open item is closed the
# same way (#20).
!data/penguin_original.ply

# ── and nothing under evidence/ is ever ignored ─────────────────────────────
# Evidence is copied in and pinned by sha256; none of it is generated here, so an
# extension-based rule has no business matching any of it. This negation is not
# hypothetical tidiness: a blanket `*.png` briefly lived above and shadowed the
# six vendored characterisation figures. They survived only because they had been
# committed before the rule was added — a fresh `git add` would have dropped
# them, and the repository would have cloned without the figures Chapter 6 cites
# while every test still passed. `tests/test_suite_shape.py` now asserts this.
!evidence/**


